// @title   TropeLang Concept Library — Perceptual Registers
// @version 0.1
// @note    How an act or agent is PERCEIVED or PLAYED — the framing qualities that fill the `as` slot of
//          Perceives / Frames (`[+Perceives(target=…, as=earnest)]`). These are shared vocabulary, NOT
//          narrative-local literals: declared here so a bare `as=earnest` resolves and chases instead of
//          reading as a broken reference. Surface variants are attached as `aka` aliases (S13).
//
// Import: import "trl/concepts/registers.trl"


// =============================================================================
// PERCEPTUAL REGISTERS — the manner in which an act or agent reads
// =============================================================================

// Sincere, genuine, meant in earnest — without irony or performance.
concept earnest        [%Timeless] [+Abstract] (aka sincere, in_earnest)

// Played as theatrical display — staged to be watched, larger than life.
concept spectacle      [%Timeless] [+Abstract] (aka theatrical)

// Played for comedy — the act reads as funny rather than grave.
concept comic          [%Timeless] [+Abstract] (aka comedic)

// Apt, deserved, just-so — the outcome reads as appropriate to what came before.
concept fitting        [%Timeless] [+Abstract] (aka apt)

// Composed, unflappable — affect withheld; grace under pressure.
concept cool           [%Timeless] [+Abstract] (aka composed)

// Heightened, serious, weighted — the act reads as drama, not farce.
concept dramatic       [%Timeless] [+Abstract] (aka heightened)

// Framed as the wronged party — the one to whom harm is done.
concept victim         [%Timeless] [+Abstract]

// Framed as the one who strikes first — the initiator of harm.
concept aggressor      [%Timeless] [+Abstract]

// A trusted member working from within — loyalty worn as cover.
concept loyal_insider  [%Timeless] [+Abstract] (aka insider)

// Left open — a question or beat deliberately not resolved.
concept unanswered     [%Timeless] [+Abstract]
